---
// Corrections and requests (rebuilt at CHK-B18) — /request-a-review. This route SURVIVES the
// cutover because it is the one the whole site promises: every remedy page, every product page,
// the brand pages and how-we-grade all say "tell us" and point here. Deleting it would break a
// promise the site makes on almost every page.
//
// The old version was rewritten rather than re-skinned: its copy routed to five pages that die
// at cutover (/tiers, /lens, /compare, /label-checker, /when-to-see-a-doctor). The FORM is kept
// as-is — it posts to /api/nominate, works with JavaScript off, and is real. Nothing here
// promises a reply or a turnaround we can't keep (the real-promises rule).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import ReviewNominateForm from '../components/ReviewNominateForm.astro';
import SafetyCallout from '../components/evidence/SafetyCallout.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Tell us we're wrong, or ask us to look at something | Somnary"
  description="Report an error on a page, or ask us to assess a product or ingredient we don't cover yet."
  contain={false}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumb trail={[{ label: 'Somnary', href: '/' }]} current="Corrections and requests" />

    <h1>Tell us we're wrong</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      Formulations change, papers get retracted, and we make mistakes like anyone else. If a
      number, a link, or a claim looks wrong, this is where to say so — and if we cover something
      you were hoping to find and don't, say that too.
    </p>

    {/* The one thing this form must never become. Stated up front, not buried under it. */}
    <SafetyCallout level="caution" title="Not the place for a personal health question">
      We can't advise on your situation, your medication, or your dose — and we shouldn't try. A
      pharmacist can see your history and answer in minutes. Please don't include personal health
      details in the form below.
    </SafetyCallout>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2>What helps most</h2>
      <ul class="tips">
        <li><strong>Which page.</strong> The address of the page you were reading, if you have it.</li>
        <li><strong>What's wrong.</strong> The specific number, link or sentence — not just "this seems off".</li>
        <li><strong>What it should say,</strong> if you know, and where you found that.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">
        Corrections are made on the page they affect, and the page's last-checked date moves when
        we make one.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2>The form</h2>
      <ReviewNominateForm />
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2>What happens next — honestly</h2>
      <p class="body">
        It goes into the queue of things to check. We read everything that comes in. We can't
        promise an individual reply, and we won't put a turnaround time here that we'd miss —
        a request is not a grade, and asking for one doesn't move anything up the list.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        Nobody pays us to look at anything, and nobody can pay to be looked at sooner.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  /* raw-ok: --page-max as a layout width — a form and its explanation are a reading column. */
  .wrap {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--page-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-5) var(--space-9);
  }
  h1 {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--display-md);
    font-weight: var(--weight-title);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
  }
  .intro {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .sec {
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-heading);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }
  .tips {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .tips li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }
  .tips strong {
    font-weight: var(--weight-strong);
  }
  .body,
  .note {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    color: var(--text-body);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .note {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
